"tk", "name": "Turkmen"}, "word": "göriplik"}, {"language": {"code": "tk", "name": "Turkmen"}, "word": "göripçilik"}, {"language": {"code": "uk", "name": "Ukrainian"}, "word": "за́здрість"}, {"language": {"code": "uk", "name": "Ukrainian"}, "word": "за́висть"}, {"language": {"code": "ur", "name": "Urdu"}, "word": "حَسَد"}, {"language": {"code": "ur", "name": "Urdu"}, "word": "اِیرْشا"}, {"language": {"code": "ur", "name": "Urdu"}, "word": "جَلَن"}, {"language": {"code": "ur", "name": "Urdu"}, "word": "اِیرْکھا"}, {"language": {"code": "ur", "name": "Urdu"}, "word": "رَشْک"}, {"language": {"code": "uz", "name": "Uzbek"}, "word": "hasad"}, {"language": {"code": "uz", "name": "Uzbek"}, "word": "rashk"}, {"language": {"code": "vi", "name": "Vietnamese"}, "word": "sự thèm muốn"}, {"language": {"code": "vi", "name": "Vietnamese"}, "word": "sự ghen tị"}, {"language": {"code": "cy", "name": "Welsh"}, "word": "eiddigedd"}, {"language": {"code": "zza", "name": "Zazaki"}, "word": "peğiley"}, {"language": {"code": "zza", "name": "Zazaki"}, "word": "haset"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "An object of envious notice or feeling.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "This constitution in former days used to be the envy of the world[.]", "reference": "1843, Thomas Macaulay, Critical and Miscellaneous Essays, Carey & Hart, page 277:"}, {"text": "Blacke Foryst of Despayr, taking photos of the band\n Put 'em up on Myspace you're the envy of the land", "reference": "2008, Lich King (band), “Black Metal Sucks”, in Toxic Zombie Onslaught:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete) Hatred, enmity, ill-feeling.", "tags": ["countable", "obsolete", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Syre said laūcelot vnto Arthur by this crye that ye haue made ye wyll put vs that ben aboute yow in grete Ieopardy\n for there be many Knyghtes that haue grete enuye to vs\n therfore whan we shal mete at the daye of Iustes there wille be hard skyfte amonge vs", "reference": "1485, Sir Thomas Malory, “lij”, in Le Morte Darthur, book X:"}, {"text": "But let me tell the World,\n If he out-liue the enuie of this day,\n England did neuer owe so sweet a hope,\n So much misconstrued in his Wantonnesse.", "reference": "1598, William Shakespeare, Henry IV, Part 1:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete) Emulation; rivalry.", "tags": ["countable", "obsolete", "uncountable"], "examples": ["c. 1631-1636, John Ford, The Fancies Chaste and Noble\nSuch as cleanliness and decency\nPrompt to a virtuous envy."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete) Public odium; ill repute.", "tags": ["countable", "obsolete", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "to lay the envy of the war upon Cicero", "reference": "1611, Ben[jamin] Jonson, Catiline His Conspiracy, London: […] [William Stansby?] for Walter Burre, →OCLC, (please specify the page):"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "A red-skinned variety of eating apple.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": ["kindness"]}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈɛnvi/", "tags": []}], "forms": [{"word": "envies", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "envying", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "envied", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "envied", "tags": ["past"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "(transitive) To feel displeasure or hatred towards (someone) for their good fortune or possessions.", "tags": ["transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Moon and Kim took a cable car together to Heaven Lake, a caldera at the top of the mountain, and walked around the area with their wives and officials from both sides.\nPictures showed Moon and Kim smiling and posing with their wives, and Moon filling a bottle with water from the lake.\n“The Chinese envy us because they can’t go down to the lake from their side but we can,” Kim said.\n“We should write another chapter of history between the North and the South by reflecting our new history on this Heaven Lake.”", "reference": "2018 September 20, Hyonhee Shin, Joyce Lee, Soyoung Kim, Haejin Choi, Pyongyang Press Corps., “Fulfilling a dream, South Korea's Moon visits sacred North Korean mountain with Kim”, in Lincoln Feast, editor, Reuters, archived from the original on 13 Nov 2018, World News:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(transitive) To resentfully or discontentedly desire (something someone else has that one lacks).", "tags": ["transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete, intransitive) To have envious feelings (at).", "tags": ["intransitive", "obsolete"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "I do not envy at their wealth, titles, offices;[…]let me live quiet and at ease.", "reference": "1624, Democritus Junior [pseudonym; Robert Burton], The Anatomy of Melancholy: […], 2nd edition, Oxford, Oxfordshire: […] John Lichfield and James Short, for Henry Cripps, →OCLC, partition II, section 3, member 3:"}, {"text": "Who envy at the prosperity of the wicked?", "reference": "1651, Jer[emy] Taylor, The Rule and Exercises of Holy Living. […], 2nd edition, London: […] Francis Ashe […], →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete, transitive) To give (something) to (someone) grudgingly or reluctantly; to begrudge.", "tags": ["obsolete", "transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "But that sweet Cordiall, which can restore\n A loue-sick hart, she did to him enuy[…].", "reference": "1590, Edmund Spenser, “Book III, Canto V”, in The Faerie Queene. […], London: […] [John Wolfe] for William Ponsonbie, →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete) To show malice or ill will; to rail.", "tags": ["obsolete"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "He has[…]envied against the people.", "reference": "c. 1608–1609 (date written), William Shakespeare, “The Tragedy of Coriolanus”, in Mr. William Shakespeares Comedies, Histories, & Tragedies […] (First Folio), London: […] Isaac Iaggard, and Ed[ward] Blount, published 1623, →OCLC, [Act III, scene iii]:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete) To do harm to; to injure; to disparage.", "tags": ["obsolete"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "If I make a lie\n To gain your love and envy my best mistress,\n Put me against a wall.", "reference": "c. 1621, John Fletcher, Philip Massinger, “The Pilgrim”, in Comedies and Tragedies […], London: […] Humphrey Robinson, […], and for Humphrey Moseley […], published 1647, →OCLC, (please specify the act number in uppercase Roman numerals, and the scene number in lowercase Roman numerals):"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete) To hate.", "tags": ["obsolete"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Both jealous of my love, envied each other", "reference": "c. 1589–1590 (date written), Christopher Marlo[we], edited by Tho[mas] Heywood, The Famous Tragedy of the Rich Iew of Malta. […], London: […] I[ohn] B[eale] for Nicholas Vavasour, […], published 1633, →OCLC, (please specify the page):"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete) To emulate.", "tags": ["obsolete"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Let later age that noble vse enuie,\nVile rancour to auoid, and cruell surquedrie", "reference": "1590, Edmund Spenser, “Book III, Canto I”, in The Faerie Queene. […], London: […] [John Wolfe] for William Ponsonbie, →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/envy", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}